WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.480
Do you recognize these images? Probably, because&nbsp;they were all born right here on the internet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.381
part of an ever expanding modern horror&nbsp;
sub-genre: creepypasta.  

00:00:08.381 --> 00:00:13.071
The origin of some&nbsp;&nbsp;creepypastas like Siren Head can be traced to&nbsp;a precise moment in time, &nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.071 --> 00:00:18.760
unlike other more established legends that are often part of oral&nbsp;traditions and involves slowly over centuries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:24.100
Digital folklore also has the ability to change&nbsp;quickly at the whim of a single user's post or tweet.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:29.380
Even the name creepypasta comes from&nbsp;
4chan- a portmanteau of creepy and copypasta,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:34.000
aka copy and paste. The necessary gesture&nbsp;for content to go viral.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.580
Over time, creepypastas expanded to include things beyond&nbsp;user-generated tales of creepy monster sightings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:44.320
and personal experiences, and have really&nbsp;
arrived in our mainstream urban legends.

